Z||000018||Galen||02-22-2001||08:37 PM||||One last thing and I'll let this go for a while..<P> <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR><BR>"I am really not much of a Earnhardt fan, and I do admit at times we cursed at him wheather watching TV or at the track. My whole family are Ford fans. But, no matter fan or not, you have to admit he was an awesome driver if not the very best on the circuit. Period."<BR><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>I find that to be the thoughts of many. summed up very nicely.<P>also.. <A HREF="http://www.slackersguild.com/~tc/earnhardt.html" TARGET=_blank>Dale Earnhardt - In His Sons Eyes</A><P>------------------<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/galen-sig.gif"> ||||reg||1
Z||000019||LarryB||02-23-2001||12:21 AM||||I saw an ad on TV earlier tonight for the "Dale Earnhardt" clock, the usual Ronco late-night-TV-type sales pitch, meow meow 'for the racing enthusiast' meow meow.<P>The fact that people can be so tacky as to try to capitalize on something like this for their own personal profit is sickening. It didn't take long for the sharks to circle.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/frown.gif"> ||||reg||8
